  "caption": {
    "text": "Anthropic has merged Project Glasswing into an expanded Cyber Verification Program that gives vetted security teams fewer cyber blocks on its newest Claude models.\n\nThe program now has three tiers: Defense Access, Red Team Access and Specialized Access. Each includes Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5 and Claude Mythos 5.1. Anthropic says its public models block most cyber work because cybersecurity is dual use, meaning the same skills can help defenders or attackers. Specialized Access has the fewest blocks and is limited to verified organizations reviewed in depth with the US government.\n\nAnthropic says Glasswing partners found at least 129,000 verified software vulnerabilities between April and July 2026, and uses that to justify wider access. It also says the figures are likely an undercount. No outside check of the numbers or of its CyScenarioBench test results was found. Members must also allow data retention so Anthropic can monitor for misuse.\n\nWould you trust a company to decide who gets the most capable AI for security work?\n\nFollow Helios for the next update on how Anthropic's cyber access plays out.",
